type: result
payload:
  requestId: req-20260811T145303Z-3bfc
  result:
    id: PLAN-ZIPMEDIA-001
    title: Zip archives as virtual folders for disk/tape/cart media
    section: Media
    priority: high
    done: false
    estimate: 3d
    description:
    - Support zip archives of disk, tape, and cartridge media as a virtual folder so users can run software without extracting zips to disk.
    - Attach/browse path accepts a .zip (or entry path inside a zip) and presents contained media as a read-only virtual directory.
    - Host attach UX (Avalonia/Xbox/console) and MediaService paths should resolve zip-backed entries the same as loose files where possible.
    - Prefer zero-copy or stream-based open of D64/G64/TAP/CRT/PRG/raw cart images from zip entries; avoid permanent extract to temp when feasible.
    - Document limitations (write-back, nested zips, multi-file loaders) and add focused tests with sample zip fixtures.
    technicalDetails:
    - Byrd TDD; red tests first for path resolution and stream open.
    - Do not invent media formats; zip is a container only over existing image types.
    - Determinism and lockstep hosts must still accept plain filesystem paths.
    - Write-back into zip is out of scope for v1 unless explicitly scoped later.
    implementationTasks:
    - task: Capture FR/TR/TEST for zip virtual media folder and attach path
      done: false
    - task: Design IMediaSource / virtual folder abstraction over zip entries
      done: false
    - task: Implement zip entry stream open for disk, tape, and cart attach
      done: false
    - task: Wire Avalonia and Xbox attach UI to accept .zip and entry pick
      done: false
    - task: Add unit/integration tests with fixture zips (no extract required)
      done: false
    - task: Update USER-GUIDE and handoff with usage and limits
      done: false
    remaining: Not started
    dependsOn: &o0 []
    functionalRequirements: *o0
    technicalRequirements: *o0
  deprecated: true

